      "content": "I hear you on the SOPs, but let's be real for a second—if we're looking at long-term scalability, is there a reason why we see such a consistent pattern where Western companies have to implement much more \"hands-on\" or \"strict\" oversight in Africa and SE Asia compared to, say, Europe? Is it just the training infrastructure, or is there something about the local work culture or even the mindset regarding professional discipline that makes those regions temperamentally different when it comes to high-pressure manufacturing? I want to make sure I'm not misreading the data on whether these regions are actually capable of the same level of autonomy as European workers.",
